    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 25 tests pass, including the new `Cp15Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**The rule:** `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field in its JSON output (consistent with the existing derived fields like `displayName`, `customerCode`, and `namesakeCount`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the tier:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nThis fits the existing pattern where `namesakeCount` is persisted at creation time and derived presentation fields are computed in the mapper on serialization. Since the endpoint normalizes an absent email to `null`, both the `SILVER` (unique + email) and `BRONZE` (no email) test cases resolve correctly. The full suite (25 tests) passes.",
